systars is a modern reimplementation of SYSTARS, a CAD tool for the synthesis
and analysis of VLSI systolic/wavefront arrays (E. T. L. Omtzigt, Delft
University of Technology, 1988). See docs/architecture/lineage.md for the
methods it builds on and their references.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Gemmini
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

systars began as a Python plan modelled on Gemmini
(https://github.com/ucb-bar/gemmini). systars is written from scratch in
Amaranth and translates no Gemmini code, but parts of its design follow
Gemmini: the PE / PEArray / SystolicArray hierarchy (Gemmini's PE, Tile and
Mesh), the SystolicConfig parameter set, the load/execute/store controller
split and the StreamReader/StreamWriter DMA engines, the execute command set
(CONFIG, PRELOAD, COMPUTE, COMPUTE_ACCUMULATE), the local address encoding
(src/systars/memory/local_addr.py) and the accumulator, which the Combiner
(src/systars/memory/combiner.py) has since replaced. Gemmini's license follows verbatim, from
ucb-bar/gemmini at commit b82d49cca798a59f010488a6f6de7243f0616536.

